:: PCIE4:   [net4F] MAC chip id: TCR=0x57100f00 xid=0x541 (recorded on this bench = 0x541, RTL8111H class) [MATCH] — the NET-4y RX-mode value (RX128_INT_EN|RX_MULTI_EN|RX_DMA_BURST|RX_EARLY_OFF) is that family's; a MISMATCH means it is the WRONG family's RX mode ::
:: PCIE4:   rings up: RX @ 0x80000000 (32 desc) TX @ 0x80020000 (8 desc); TCR readback 0x57100f00 (live); CPlusCmd 0x2020 PCIDAC=0 (expected clear; 64-bit DMA rides the descriptor addr) ::
:: PCIE4:   [net5R] ARMED: rx-desc[1..31].addr re-pointed from rx-bufs 0x80010000 to SHADOW 0x80050000 (NC window +0x50000, 65536 B, tag idx 0x80..) AFTER RxEnb; slot 0 left on its own buffer as the control. Re-point readback (NC direct DRAM): rx-desc[1].addr=0x80050800 expect=0x80050800 rx-desc[17].addr=0x80058800 expect=0x80058800 [MATCH] — NO descriptor carries buffer 17's address (0x80018800) any more, so a later landing THERE is an address the NIC holds internally ::
