:: PCIE4:   [net4F] rx[0] slot=0 len=342 own-buffer-written=yes buffers-written(count=1)=[0,-1,-1,-1] — the payload IS in the completed slot's own buffer -> per-descriptor addressing WORKS ::
:: PCIE4:   [net5T] rx[0] slot=0 len=342 UNREAD-LANDINGS shadow-mask=0x00000000 (first=-1) ring-mask=0x00000001 (first=0) own-shadow=0 own-ring=1 slot_expected=0 slot_read=0 unread=0 read_len=-1 verdict=CONTROL-OK — the CONTROL slot's own buffer was written — desc[0] is the one descriptor `net5_arm` deliberately leaves on its original address, so this is the control landing correctly and says NOTHING about prefetch depth (render8 scored it PREFETCHED, which both invented a prefetch depth of 1 and, by making PREFETCHED non-zero, disarmed the NOWHERE ⇒ C1 rule) ::
